From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: tag_vsc73xx_8021q: do not assume a marked
 frame's port is bridged

vsc73xx_xmit() handles a frame marked for TX forwarding offload by
looking up the port's bridge and passing it to br_vlan_enabled(), which
dereferences it. Frames are only marked while the port offloads
forwarding for its bridge, but a marked frame can still reach the tagger
after the port left the bridge, for example from a qdisc installed on
the user port, and dsa_port_bridge_dev_get() and
dsa_port_bridge_num_get() each read dp->bridge again while
dsa_port_bridge_destroy() may be clearing it.

Read dp->bridge once, and send a marked frame for a port without a
bridge like an unmarked one: on the port's standalone VLAN, out of that
port only.

tag_sja1105 (sja1105_imprecise_xmit()) and tag_dsa make the same
assumption about marked frames and would need the same treatment; they
are not used on the target this was written for.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c | 20 +++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

--- a/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
+++ b/net/dsa/tag_vsc73xx_8021q.c
@@ -17,13 +17,19 @@ vsc73xx_xmit(struct sk_buff *skb, struct net_device *netdev)
 	u8 pcp;
 
 	if (skb->offload_fwd_mark) {
-		unsigned int bridge_num = dsa_port_bridge_num_get(dp);
-		struct net_device *br = dsa_port_bridge_dev_get(dp);
-
-		if (br_vlan_enabled(br))
-			return skb;
-
-		tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge_num);
+		/* Frames are marked only while the port offloads forwarding
+		 * for its bridge, but a marked frame can still reach the port
+		 * after it left the bridge, e.g. from a qdisc. Read the bridge
+		 * once and send such a frame like an unmarked one.
+		 */
+		const struct dsa_bridge *bridge = READ_ONCE(dp->bridge);
+
+		if (bridge) {
+			if (br_vlan_enabled(bridge->dev))
+				return skb;
+
+			tx_vid = dsa_tag_8021q_bridge_vid(bridge->num);
+		}
 	}
 
 	pcp = netdev_txq_to_tc(netdev, queue_mapping);
